{
  "tema": 6000,
  "slug": "subjuntivo-presente-yo-go",
  "titulo": "Conjugate yo-go verbs in the present subjunctive",
  "subtitulo": "Tengo → tenga. The g from yo stays in every person.",
  "foto": "t06.jpg",
  "regla": "If the present-tense yo form ends in -go, the g stays through the whole subjunctive, with -er / -ir endings: tenga, tengas, tengamos.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Some irregular verbs have a **yo** form ending in **-go** in the present: **tengo, vengo, pongo, hago, digo, salgo, traigo, oigo, caigo**. To form the subjunctive, **take that stem with the g and keep it through the whole conjugation**. The endings are the same as for regular **-er** and **-ir** verbs."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "**yo** form in **-go**",
            "minus **-o**",
            "**-a, -as, -a, -amos, -an**"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "tener",
            "venir"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "tenga",
              "venga"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "tengas",
              "vengas"
            ],
            [
              "él, ella, usted",
              "tenga",
              "venga"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros",
              "tengamos",
              "vengamos"
            ],
            [
              "ustedes, ellos",
              "tengan",
              "vengan"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Verb",
            "Present **yo**",
            "Subjunctive"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "poner",
              "pongo",
              "ponga"
            ],
            [
              "hacer",
              "hago",
              "haga"
            ],
            [
              "decir",
              "digo",
              "diga"
            ],
            [
              "salir",
              "salgo",
              "salga"
            ],
            [
              "traer",
              "traigo",
              "traiga"
            ],
            [
              "oír",
              "oigo",
              "oiga"
            ],
            [
              "caer",
              "caigo",
              "caiga"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: the **g** is a tattoo. Once **yo** has it, everyone keeps it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "No ==tengas== miedo, aquí estoy.",
              "en": "Don't be afraid, I'm here."
            },
            {
              "es": "No ==vengan== después de las diez.",
              "en": "Don't come any later than ten. (to several people)"
            },
            {
              "es": "Es mejor que ==pongas== los vasos en el lavaplatos.",
              "en": "It's best if you put the glasses in the dishwasher."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Hagamos== lo correcto.",
              "en": "Let's do the right thing."
            },
            {
              "es": "Conviene que ==traigan== las sombrillas a la playa.",
              "en": "It'd be good for them to bring the umbrellas to the beach."
            },
            {
              "es": "Ojalá ==tengan== suerte y consigan el trabajo.",
              "en": "I hope you're lucky and get the job."
            },
            {
              "es": "Quiero que me ==digas== la verdad.",
              "en": "I want you to tell me the truth."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The **g** doesn't stay only in **yo**. And the form isn't built from the infinitive."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Ojalá que tienen suerte."
                },
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Ojalá que tenan suerte."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Ojalá que tengan suerte."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Not the ordinary present, and not without the **g**."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Quiero que hacemos la carne asada."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Quiero que hagamos la carne asada."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "**Hago** → **hagamos**. The **g** goes with **nosotros** too."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Es mejor que sales temprano."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Es mejor que salgas temprano."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
